<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">10 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 10 February, from 1258 to 1989.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1258</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Baghdad surrenders to the Mongols</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a short siege, the Abbasid Caliph al-Musta'sim surrendered Baghdad to Hulagu Khan. The city was sacked and the Caliph executed days later, ending five centuries of Abbasid rule from Baghdad.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hulagu-khan">Hulagu Khan</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1306</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert the Bruce kills John Comyn at Dumfries</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Bruce stabbed his rival for the Scottish crown before the altar of Greyfriars church. Committed to rebellion, he was crowned King of Scots weeks later and defeated the English at Bannockburn in 1314.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1763</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Treaty of Paris ends the Seven Years' War</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">France ceded Canada and lands east of the Mississippi to Britain, and Spain gave up Florida. Britain emerged as the leading colonial power, though France kept its trading posts in India.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1840</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Queen Victoria marries Prince Albert</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Victoria married her cousin Albert of Saxe-Coburg and Gotha at the Chapel Royal, St James's Palace. Her white wedding dress set a lasting fashion; Albert became her closest adviser.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1906</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">HMS Dreadnought is launched</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King Edward VII launched the battleship at Portsmouth. With ten 12-inch guns and steam turbines, she made existing battleships obsolete and intensified the naval race with Germany.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1940</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet Union begins mass deportations from eastern Poland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The NKVD deported some 140,000 Polish citizens, many of them families of settlers and foresters, to Siberia and Kazakhstan. It was the first of four mass deportations in 1940-41.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1962</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">U-2 pilot Gary Powers exchanged for Soviet spy Rudolf Abel</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the Glienicke Bridge between West Berlin and Potsdam, the US pilot shot down in 1960 was swapped for the KGB colonel Rudolf Abel. The bridge became known for Cold War exchanges.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1989</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ron Brown becomes the first Black chairman of a major US party</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ron Brown was elected chairman of the Democratic National Committee. He helped Bill Clinton win in 1992 and became Secretary of Commerce before dying in a plane crash in 1996.</p></li></ol>
